{"id": "tpl-mmm-fy2024-opex-structure", "set": "templates", "question": "On 3M's consolidated statement of income for fiscal year 2024, which expense line items make up total operating expenses, what is the amount of each, and what operating income results from net sales less total operating expenses? Give amounts in millions of USD.", "gold_type": "text", "gold": "Total operating expenses of $19,753 million comprise three non-zero line items in 2024: cost of sales $14,447 million; selling, general and administrative expenses $4,221 million; and research, development and related expenses $1,085 million. The statement also presents Gain on business divestitures and Goodwill impairment expense, both shown as zero (\u2014) for 2024 (goodwill impairment was $271 million in 2022). Net sales of $24,575 million less total operating expenses of $19,753 million gives operating income of $4,822 million.", "tier": "T1", "stratum": "structure", "category": "structure", "rubric": ["Cost of sales is $14,447 million", "Selling, general and administrative expenses are $4,221 million", "Research, development and related expenses are $1,085 million", "Total operating expenses are $19,753 million", "Operating income is $4,822 million"], "gold_source": "document-read", "filing": {"cik": "0000066740", "accession": "0000066740-25-000006", "ticker": "MMM", "fiscal_year": 2024, "form": "10-K"}, "notes": "Gold read from the consolidated statement of income; confirmed by hand by the author 2026-09-03. Rubric re-authored after the first judged run (2026-09-03): a contradiction test phrased as a rubric point inverted the score, and the gold's 'three line items' penalized answers that faithfully listed the statement's two zero lines. Structure stratum: the calculation linkbase says what sums to OperatingIncomeLoss; rung 5 (OIM) carries no calculation network, so the model must infer the roll-up from concept names alone. Tagged us-gaap:CostOfGoodsAndServicesSold, us-gaap:SellingGeneralAndAdministrativeExpense, mmm:ResearchDevelopmentAndRelatedExpenses, us-gaap:OperatingExpenses, us-gaap:OperatingIncomeLoss.", "contradictions": ["For 2024 the only non-zero operating expense line items are cost of sales ($14,447 million), SG&A ($4,221 million) and research, development and related expenses ($1,085 million); total operating expenses are $19,753 million and operating income is $4,822 million. Any other 2024 operating expense line item is zero."]}
{"id": "tpl-mmm-fy2024-pfas-exit", "set": "templates", "question": "According to 3M's fiscal year 2024 Form 10-K, by when does 3M plan to exit all PFAS manufacturing, approximately how many positions were impacted by the related workforce actions that management approved and committed to during 2024, and what pre-tax charge did those 2024 actions produce?", "gold_type": "text", "gold": "3M announced in 2022 that it will exit all PFAS manufacturing by the end of 2025. During 2024, management approved and committed to additional related workforce actions impacting approximately 650 positions, resulting in a pre-tax charge of $66 million, primarily impacting cost of sales and reflected within the Transportation and Electronics business segment. (The 2023 actions had produced a $64 million pre-tax charge; the initiative has impacted approximately 1,200 positions worldwide since 2023.)", "tier": "T1", "stratum": "lookup", "category": "narrative", "rubric": ["3M plans to exit all PFAS manufacturing by the end of 2025", "The workforce actions approved and committed to in 2024 impacted approximately 650 positions", "The 2024 actions resulted in a pre-tax charge of $66 million", "The charge primarily impacted cost of sales"], "gold_source": "document-read", "filing": {"cik": "0000066740", "accession": "0000066740-25-000006", "ticker": "MMM", "fiscal_year": 2024, "form": "10-K"}, "notes": "Gold read from Note 6 (Restructuring Actions, '2023 to 2025 PFAS Exit Actions'); confirmed by hand by the author 2026-09-03. Narrative question: on rung 7a the path is search-documents then get-document-section (a second fetch, logged as its own cost line); on the in-context rungs the passage is in the document. The $64M (2023) versus $66M (2024) pair is one confusable; the neighbouring '2023 to 2025 Structural Reorganization Actions' paragraph (1,100 positions, $187 million) is the other, and two graph rungs took it on the first run. Rubric re-authored after that run: the contradiction test is a statement, not a rubric point.", "contradictions": ["The PFAS-exit workforce actions approved and committed to during 2024 impacted approximately 650 positions and produced a pre-tax charge of $66 million (the 2023 actions produced $64 million); 3M exits all PFAS manufacturing by the end of 2025. Figures from other restructuring programs in the same note (for example approximately 1,100 positions and $187 million for the 2023 to 2025 Structural Reorganization Actions) are not the PFAS-exit figures."]}
